  "model_policy": [
    "Complete source raw uint16 fields are not bounded by familiar AC presets. Integer32 numeric tokens store low16. Strict integer/string validation and atomic rejection deliberately avoid native coercion, memory faults and partial mutation.",
    "WB04A operation dispatch requires inner t to be a string before registry lookup; arrays and objects are rejected atomically as InvalidPacket. This is safe emulator parsing, not a claimed firmware result: CatalogQuirks/WB/assessment.json records the WB04 registry table at 0x1000121c and its nine named operations, but does not qualify non-string t behavior. The Python TypeError is an emulator bug, not a firmware fault.",
    "All additional raw reports start at explicitly synthetic0, not source or mainboard defaults. Existing synthetic AC sensors refresh on thermal advance. Platform metadata uses synthetic name/MID, zero lock/update/availability, fixed clock, RSSI-50 and otherwise empty mainboard buffers.",
    "Local metadata callbacks precede numeric table, including string FaultDisplay on RT13 but numeric FaultDisplay on WB04. DevID/MafIdf consume successful columns without appending values, matching the original callback.",
    "Metadata commands partition before numeric commands in res opt/p. name/ModelType/AppTimer setters do not change reports. ReportClientID stores only a local synthetic report target; it has no status getter and contributes no p member.",
    "PR148867993/c4b744 independently decoded exact table and original mutation/status loops; they are not aliases of historicalc9/e1 payloads."
  ],
